From e467908f86a882c23ae66da00807fd6e0101350d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Purvis <mike.purvis@simberobotics.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:46:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Build vendored DART as C++17

DART sets no language standard before 6.20 (dartsim/dart#3505), so a
compiler that defaults to C++20, such as GCC 16, builds it as C++20.
Its implicit [=] captures of this are deprecated there, and DART's
-Werror turns that into an error.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Rz4Zs3SLnKowSZhUs8Yrme
Epiq-Ref: HWMHQWJ
Signed-off-by: Mike Purvis <mike.purvis@simberobotics.com>
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 2b2374e..aaa861a 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -43,6 +43,9 @@ ament_vendor(${PROJECT_NAME}
     -DDART_BUILD_GUI_OSG:BOOL=FALSE
     -DDART_BUILD_DARTPY:BOOL=FALSE
     -DDART_BUILD_EXTRAS:BOOL=FALSE
+    # DART before 6.20 sets no language standard, so compilers that default to
+    # C++20 (GCC 16) reject its implicit [=] captures of this under -Werror.
+    -DCMAKE_CXX_STANDARD:STRING=17
   GLOBAL_HOOK
   PATCHES patches
 )
-- 
